# irodoriAnimation(Player player)
# irodori animation
#
# Driver for the colour burst. Timeline, in ticks from the start — this
# reproduces the original hand-unrolled version exactly, it is just
# written as a schedule instead of hidden in `@if i == 18` checks
# halfway down a loop body:
#
#   t=0    scatter, instant     + burst A, pitch 0.5 -> 0.9
#   t=36   scatter, 2t per block
#   t=72                          burst B, pitch 0.9 -> 1.3
#   t=106  scatter, 2t per block
#   t=142                         burst C, pitch 1.3 -> 1.7
#
# Every pass after the first is fired with @console so it runs alongside
# the ones already in flight — the ring is being emptied while the
# previous burst is still flying home. That is why the passes live in
# irodoriAnimation:: functions and every command inside them is wrapped in
# `execute in {{animWorld}}`: console has no world of its own.
#
# The three pitch windows butt up against each other (0.5-0.9, 0.9-1.3,
# 1.3-1.7) and moveBlockDisplays ramps linearly inside each one, so the
# chime climbs smoothly from 0.5 to 1.7 across all 105 blocks instead of
# resetting to a random pitch every pass. To retune the whole animation,
# move those six numbers; to change its shape, move the delays. Keep the
# delays summing the same way if you change stepTicks in
# irodoriAnimation.nms — 35 displays * stepTicks is one pass.
#
# Requires irodoriAnimation::summonBlockDisplays() to have been run once in-world.
@using irodoriAnimation
@fast

@console function execute irodoriAnimation::dyeArmourGradient("{{armorStandUuid}}")
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::shakeStand("{{armorStandUuid}}", Player("{{player.getName()}}"))
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::spiralParticles("{{armorStandUuid}}")

@var scatterBlockDisplays(0)
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::moveBlockDisplays(Player("{{player.getName()}}"), Double(0.5D), Double(0.9D), 0)

@delay 36
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::scatterBlockDisplays({{stepTicks}})

@delay 36
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::moveBlockDisplays(Player("{{player.getName()}}"), Double(0.9D), Double(1.3D), 72)

@delay 34
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::scatterBlockDisplays({{stepTicks}})

@delay 36
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::moveBlockDisplays(Player("{{player.getName()}}"), Double(1.3D), Double(1.7D), 142)

# t=176. interpolationTicks after the final pass began, which is the tick
# its first display lands. vanishBlockDisplays then walks the ring at the
# same stepTicks cadence, so each one shrinks away exactly as it settles.
@delay 34
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::vanishBlockDisplays()

# t=250. The last display starts shrinking at 244 and is gone by 250, the
# armour fade and the colour spiral both end at 240, and shakeStand has
# set the child back on the ground at 240 — so this is the first tick with
# nothing else running. Bang.
@delay 54
@console function execute irodoriAnimation::finale(Player("{{player.getName()}}"))
